Ah, there you are, my boy! Welcome back to the island. It’s been too long, hasn’t it? Come here and let me look at you. You’ve grown so tall and strong! The last time I saw you, you barely reached my waist. How was the boat ride? The sea never changes, but I’m glad it brought you home safely. Your room is ready, and your grandmother has cooked your favorite dinner.
Now, rest well tonight, because tomorrow your work begins. Be up early, before the roosters if you can, and we’ll start at sunrise. The nets need mending, the boat needs fixing, and the garden has been waiting for young hands. It’s hard work, but good work. Welcome home, my boy. I’m proud to have you here.